  "published": "2026-07-07T06:40:38.68Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING: core types moved from ResultCrafter.Core.Primitives to the ResultCrafter namespace; Minimal API extensions moved to ResultCrafter.AspNetCore, controller extensions to ResultCrafter.AspNetCore.Mvc; Result<T>.Ok / Created / Accepted now require a non-null value ([MemberNotNullWhen] makes Value flow-safe after an IsSuccess check). Fixed: controller To*Result error responses and the EF Core concurrency handler now set the HTTP transport status code (previously sent as 200 / 500 with a correct ProblemDetails body); ALL To*Result methods now enforce SuccessKind. Added: ErrorType.Gone (410), UnprocessableEntity (422), TooManyRequests (429) with factories, attributes, and builder extensions; Result.Match / Result<T>.Match; DebuggerDisplay on both Result structs. Error.BadRequest merges field-error keys differing only by case. EF Core dependency floors are open minimums (8.0.0 / 9.0.0 / 10.0.0). Packages marked AOT/trim-compatible (except ResultCrafter.MediatR).",
